{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the County of Tripolis ruler from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was born around 1130 and was the son of Ponce II the Handsome and the brother of Raymond II the Wise. \nRaymond III married to Esclarmonde de Moncada who was from the powerful de Moncada family. \nIn 1152 Raymond III took control of the County of Tripolis after the death of his brother Raymond II the Wise. \nHe expanded the County of Tripolis borders by marrying to the daughter of Prince Bohemond I of Antioch. \nIn the 1150s Raymond III led the County of Tripolis army against the Fatimid Caliphate. \nHe was a Christian leader in the 12th century and was part of the Crusades. \nRaymond III died in 1187 in the Battle of Hattin. \nHe was killed by Saladin.\n\n**Conquest of Jerusalem**\nRaymond III led the County of Tripolis army against the Fatimid Caliphate. \nHe was defeated at the Battle of Hattin. \nThe Crusaders lost the Battle of Hattin and Saladin captured Jerusalem. \nRaymond III was captured by Saladin and executed in Acre. \nThe County of Tripolis surrendered to Saladin after the death of Raymond III.\n\n**Family**\nRaymond III married to Esclarmonde de Moncada in 1141. \nEsclarmonde was from the powerful de Moncada family and was the daughter of Tancrède II. \nRaymond III had one son with Esclarmonde named Raymond IV. \nRaymond IV became the Count of Tripolis after the death of his father. \n\n**See also**\nRaymond III Count of Tripolis was a ruler in the County of Tripolis during the 12th century. \nHe was a Christian leader during the Crusades. \nRaymond III died in 1187 in the Battle of Hattin. \nHe was killed by Saladin.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0013606823049485683}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001284993631998077}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.19242680072784